  "Paid": "Amount, method, timestamp. No green badge — paid is the expected case and colouring it makes the unpaid row harder to find.",
  "Pending": "“Sent to the bank, usually clears within an hour.” Never “processing” alone — a duration prevents the second attempt that causes a double charge.",
  "Failed": "Reason in plain words (“the card expired”), what was NOT affected (“access is unchanged”), and the single recovery action. Never a provider error code as the headline.",
  "Retrying": "Attempt number, next attempt time, and how to stop it. A silent retry loop is how a member gets charged three times.",
  "Overdue": "Amount, days late, and whether access is affected under this tenant's policy — the answer differs per tenant and must never be inferred by the reader.",
  "Refunded": "Signed amount, destination, arrival window, reason, and who authorised it. All five, always.",
  "Partially refunded": "Both figures side by side — original and refunded — never a single net number that hides what happened.",
  "Disputed": "What the member claims, the evidence deadline, and who owns the response. Time-boxed, so the deadline is the loudest element.",
  "Cash pending": "“Collected at the desk, not yet reconciled.” Distinguishes a drawer variance from a real shortfall at close.",
  "Wallet applied": "Credit used and remaining balance, both visible. A wallet with an invisible balance is a support ticket."
